-- title:
--   Unique place of the disc inducing a given section
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0 \subseteq L \subseteq F$ be a tower of fields with $L$ algebraically closed of characteristic $0$ and $F$ a curve over $L$ (principal divisors exist, residue fields of places are finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank $1$), let $F_0$ be a $k_0$-subextension of $F$ with $k_0(\mathrm{im}\,L) \sqcup F_0 = F$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$, $\bar F$ a field over the residue field of $A$, and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residues in $\bar F$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, with a surjective residue map to $\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue). Let $K_1 \subseteq L$ be a $k_0$-subextension with $L/K_1$ algebraic, $A_1$ the valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$, whose residue map onto the residue field of $A$ is assumed surjective; write $F_1 = k_0(\mathrm{im}\,K_1) \sqcup F_0$. Let $S_1$ be a subring of $F$, $\varphi_1 : A_1[X] \to S_1$ and $\chi_1 : S_1 \to \kappa(A)$ ring homomorphisms, and $D_1$ a set of places of $F$ over $L$ (valuation subrings, proper, containing $L$, principal ideal rings), characterised by: $P \in D_1$ iff $P$ is rational (i.e. $L \to \kappa(P)$ is surjective), every $f \in S_1$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for all $f \in S_1$ one has $\mathrm{val}_A(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)) < 1$ iff $\chi_1 f = 0$. Assume: $A_1$ maps into $S_1$, $\varphi_1$ agrees on constants with this map, $\chi_1 \circ \varphi_1 \circ C$ is the residue map of $A_1$, and $\chi_1(\varphi_1 X) = 0$; $\varphi_1 X \neq \varphi_1(C\,c)$ for all $c \in A_1$; $S_1$ is local with maximal ideal $\ker \chi_1$, Noetherian and a unique factorisation domain; $S_1 \subseteq F_1$ and every element of $F_1$ is a quotient of elements of $S_1$ with nonzero denominator; elements of $L$ linearly independent over $K_1$ remain linearly independent over $F_1$ in the sense that $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ with $a_i \in F_1$ forces all $a_i = 0$; every proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $L$ is a principal ideal ring; $\varpi \neq 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_1$ and $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_1$; for $f \in F_1$, $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in S_1$ and $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$; every ring homomorphism $S_1 \to A_1$ fixing $A_1$ and reducing to $\chi_1$ has kernel generated by $\varphi_1 X - \varphi_1(C(\chi(\varphi_1 X)))$; and every prime $p$ of $S_1$ not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ divides, for each $x \in S_1$, the value at $x$ of some monic polynomial over $A_1$ pushed through $\varphi_1 \circ C$. Then for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_1 \to A_1$ with $\chi(\varphi_1(C\,a)) = a$ for $a \in A_1$ and with residue $\chi_1$, there is exactly one place $P$ of $F$ over $L$ with $P \in D_1$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ in $L$ for all $f \in S_1$.
--
--   This is the statement that, in the local frame attached to a smooth point of the reduction, each $A_1$-valued section of the local ring $S_1$ lifting $\chi_1$ is realised by a unique place of the disc $D_1$: existence comes from the branch place attached to the prime $\ker\chi$, uniqueness from the rationality of the induced discrete valuation on the level field. It is the clause of the smooth-point locality package [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint) asserting the existence and uniqueness of sections, and uses the two branch-place results `exists_prime_forall_evalAt_eq_zero_iff_dvd_of_mem_disc` and `exists_mem_disc_forall_evalAt_eq_zero_iff_dvd_of_prime` together with the uniqueness of extensions of rational discrete valuations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_existsUnique_mem_disc_forall_evalAt_eq_of_section.lean

